    `npm run lint` is `eslint .`, so every .js/.mjs under web/ is a lint
    target. The flat config only carried one rules block, `files:
    ['**/*.{ts,tsx}']`, so eslint.config.js itself and
    scripts/run-with-supported-node.mjs — the launcher the release
    verification runs `npm test` through — matched no config object and were
    linted with zero rules. They reported clean because nothing was checked:
    `calculateConfigForFile` returned 0 rules for them against 108 for a
    .ts file.

    Add a `**/*.{js,mjs}` config object extending js.configs.recommended
    (64 rules) with the Node globals those scripts use declared inline; the
    `globals` package is not a dependency and the lockfile is not
    regenerated. Nothing is loosened: no path is added to `ignores`, no rule
    is turned off, no eslint-disable is introduced, and the ts/tsx block is
    untouched. The existing .js/.mjs files already satisfy the recommended
    set, so no script needed changing.

